  "summary": "The ~200 t diesel-hydraulic backhoe excavator is the primary loading unit in the bauxite pit. It digs the friable ore (and blasted caprock) with an ~11–12 m³ bucket, swings and loads ~90 t trucks in about five to six passes. Everything moves hydraulically: the diesel drives piston pumps; joysticks pilot the control valves that feed the boom, arm and bucket cylinders, swing motors and travel motors.",
